From bfc5f0f6aa601cd205b7a84c615821f860aff6d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: ready-wait notices check the live board
 against its pulled replica (no "no worker" from a lagging copy)

Defect t_01a1d390d19239dd (2026-11-12 22:11 PST, MacBook): chat_wait_unclaimed told a chat that
t_01a1d1292db9d3cb and t_01a1d12a594c8fd7 were "ready with no worker claiming it" 30 min after the
Board completed them. After a sync-loop stall the live feed cursor (1650734) trailed the board's own
pulled replica (sync-shadow, 1713384) by ~62k rows, so the live rows still read ready, and sweep()
stated the Board fact from them with no freshness check.

- hermes_cli/kanban_replica_freshness.py (new): reads the pulled replica (cursor and the mark_pulled
  stamp kanban_chat_links already uses). lag_hold() says why Board facts must wait: live feed more
  than MAX_FEED_LAG_ROWS (2000) behind the replica, or a replica pull older than
  REPLICA_STALE_SECONDS (600). newer_rows() returns replica rows with a strictly newer sync_version
  than the live rows. Fail-open: an unsynced board, no replica or an unreadable one changes nothing.
- kanban_chat_wait.sweep(): defers every notice while lag_hold() holds (the episode keeps its
  ready@since key, so it fires once when the lag closes, if still ready), and skips a card whose
  newer replica row is no longer ready or is a later ready episode. Both log the reason.
- kanban_wake_fold._live_task() (refresh_card, #1443's claim-time relabel): the replica's status
  wins when its revision is newer than the live row's.

Tests: (a)-(c) plus a stale-pull case in test_kanban_ready_wait_checkpoint.py, (d) in
test_kanban_wake_fold.py. (a), (b), the stale-pull case and (d) fail on origin/main; dropping the
replica cross-check fails (a); dropping the lag defer fails (b) and the stale-pull case.
---
